{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/172811-overlapping-thresholds","id":172811,"title":"Overlapping Thresholds?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-18T08:11:01-07:00","id":172811,"title":"Overlapping Thresholds?","content":"So I'm trying to figure out the Threshold for a keystone, a Belgian franc damaged by artillery fire in WWI, but I'm not whether it's Death by Violence or Death by Chance. Given the intentional violent mode of harm, it seems like a natural fit for the former, but since it wasn't an attack on a specific individual it seems to fall under the latter. Is there an agreed upon way to negotiate this issue, or is it simply a matter of what seems more poetic? Thank you for your time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","name":"Wasteful","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T08:33:18-07:00","id":172828,"title":"","content":"Depends if the people firing the artillery were targeting the group he belonged to, or if he was a civilian chilling in his house and his own people blew him up in a freak accident.<br /> <br /> If he's a soldier, and was hit by an enemy mortar which was fired by someone with the intent to kill people in the army the soon-to-be-Sin-Eater was part of, then that's absolutely Death by Violence.<br /> <br /> In my opinion, at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T09:18:26-07:00","id":172889,"title":"","content":"Artillery is a weapon, fired with the intent of destroying things and killing people. Almost certainly Violence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T09:38:36-07:00","id":172916,"title":"","content":"What does your character think does he believe it was an accident caused by his allies or does he believe it was really caused by violence from the enemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T10:08:58-07:00","id":172942,"title":"","content":"Hm, he probably would have seen it as violence by the enemy. Violence it is, then! Thank you very much for your insight, everyone!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/985-wasteful","name":"Wasteful","avatar":"data:imag